## Architecture rules

- **Separate git repos and databases.** Never share DBs across products.
- Integrate via **HTTP APIs** + shared IDs (employee / client / project) — future SSO.
- MULK OS does **not** own operational data; it calls each module’s `/ecosystem/summary` with `X-Ecosystem-Key`.
- Default bridge key (local): `mulk-dev-bridge`
- Start all apps: `bash "/Users/user/Mulk Ecosystem/scripts/dev-ecosystem.sh"`

## Domain ownership

| Domain | System of record |
|--------|------------------|
| Employee unique id | HRMS |
| Clients, projects, leads | CRM |
| Production, shipping, vendors, cost | PO Tracker |

When a change must span two products: implement the API in the **owner**, document the contract, then update consumers (usually MULK OS) in their own Cursor window.
